id=axion_spsm
name=Axion Super Power Saving
version=v3.10.1
versionCode=79
author=Axion SPSM
description=v3.10.1, the device-verified reunion of the v3.9.2 race round and the perf round, with the two field bugs it caught fixed: a restore write the kernel refuses while the value ALREADY stands at its original is a no-op success, not drift (cpu6/online refused both directions on 2026-09-25 and one exit paid 70s of safety valves over a value that had returned), and gesture dispatch now defaults to the app_process input/am wrappers - the native cmd binary's binder dies in the recognizer's nohup'd root context (Failure calling service input), which is why recognised swipes went nowhere. From v3.9.2: the batch tool runs where uid 2000 can read it (KernelSU keeps /data/adb at 700 root; runtime copy in /data/local/tmp/spsm, republished every boot) and answers in milliseconds (result receiver pumped like the platform's own cmd); a deactivate landing mid-restrict no longer strands anything (journal-first records, an "applying" state the exit honours, bounded stand-down wait, unreadable values restored from record); the recognizer follows the first finger down on ANY slot. From the perf round: deep grace, native cmd paths, one JVM per batch with shell fans as fallback, swipe up = home / hold = recents while the mode owns the bottom edge.
